{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>HaTzfoni</b> Two times in the Masorah: here and the other: ואת הצפוני ארחיק מעליכם. This is that Elijah comes from the tribe of Gad, as in 1 Kings 17 he traces him with the descendants of Gad. Thus והצפוני ארחיק מעליכם — that the evil inclination will be nullified." "<b>Letzafon</b> It is Tzifyon. And written צפון — on account that Moses, who received the Ten Commandments, is צפון in his portion."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The Masorah quotation ואת הצפוני ארחיק מעליכם does not correspond to any known biblical verse; translated hyper-literally as it stands. The reference to 1 Kings 17 is Elijah's first appearance; the genealogical linking to Gad is a midrashic tradition."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:13.795290168Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}